I just made the wiki so the real contributers could determine whetherthey wanted a wiki or not.  I had a easily deployable solution so Itook the hour it took to learn how to do it and did it.
Personally I would avoid marking projects as "locked" and rather notethem as being "worked on" by people.  That would imply leaving behinda point of contact so one could determine if the project had beenabandoned/postponed/delayed.
Just my $0.02.  I haven't worked on any code in a team setting though,so that's just the intuition of a totally clean look at the situation. It may not be a viable option because of various reasons that I wasnot here to experience.
If you want to keep the wiki, I have no problem keeping it thereindefinitely.  Take your time - all my work on that domain is under awhole different area, so just have fun (and tell me if there are anywiki-settings that you would like changed.  I'll happily change themif you want them to be changed, provided you tell me how if it's alarge/complex change).
